{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Return.</b> May Your rest be here among us, as in זֹאת מְנוּחָתִי עֲדֵי עַד (Psalms 132:14). And even though You reveal Your Shekhinah before Israel to drive out their enemies, let the rest of Your Shekhinah be among us." "<b>YHWH of the myriads of thousands of Israel.</b> Like יהוה צְבָאוֹת אַלְפֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, as the Sages said (Kiddushin 76a): He is not called Tzevaot except on account of the hosts of Israel. And he says רִבְבוֹת אַלְפֵי in the manner of רִבֹּתַיִם אַלְפֵי שִׁנְאָן (Psalms 68:18), for perhaps Israel at that time reached that number, counting men, women, and children."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:18.179526888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}